The Problem: The "Are we there yet?" Trap

Imagine you are building a YouTube application. You have a YoutubeChannel class and a
Subscriber class.

The Beginner Way (Polling):
The junior developer writes code where the Subscriber uses a while(true) loop to check
the channel every 5 seconds:
"Do you have a new video? No."
"Do you have a new video? No."

Why a Senior rejects this: This is called Polling. It is a disaster. If a channel has 1
million subscribers, and they all check the server every 5 seconds, you will DDoS
attack your own server and crash the entire company.